-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
mapsicon  —  silhouettes for four microstates
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Author:    Régis Freyd
Source:    https://github.com/djaiss/mapsicon
Retrieved: 2026-09-13, all/<cc>/vector.svg at master
License:   None stated. The project's README grants, verbatim:

               Do what you want with them as long as you mention me in your
               project. Please don't resell them - I forbid it!

    Mondo is free to play and sells nothing, so the second condition is met.
    This entry, and tools/mapsicon/README.md, are how the first is met.

    Four countries take their silhouette from this artwork instead of from
    Natural Earth: Monaco, San Marino, Liechtenstein and Nauru (D-59). Natural
    Earth's 10m dataset does not resolve a country of a few square kilometres —
    Nauru is nine vertices there, Monaco twelve — and the three of them rendered
    as the same blob, which makes a question unanswerable rather than hard.

    Only the OUTLINE comes from here. Every centroid, and therefore every
    distance and compass hint the game gives, still comes from Natural Earth.
    tools/lib/icon.mjs applies the file's own transform and fits the result into
    the same 500x500 box the projected shapes use; the drawings are not modified
    beyond that and coordinate rounding.

    This is the only artwork in the build from a source without a formal
    licence. It is committed under tools/mapsicon/ rather than fetched, so its
    provenance stays legible. It is unrelated to the gitignored assets/
    directory, which is reference material of unknown origin (D-15, D-16) and
    remains barred from the build.
